From: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:10:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] qb64-classic: exit programs cleanly on Haiku instead of
 crashing on END
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The legacy runtime has the same shutdown problem as the Phoenix Edition port:
Haiku's libglut registers an exit handler that destroys the remaining GLUT
windows and calls BGLView::UnlockGL() on them, while QB64 terminates the
program from the main loop thread and leaves the window owned by the thread
inside glutMainLoop(). Every graphics program therefore died with a
"UnlockGL called without LockGL" crash report after a normal END.

Route all terminating exit() calls in libqb.cpp through QB64_QUIT(), which on
Haiku flushes and calls _exit() so the exit handlers never run. Other platforms
and console-only builds keep plain exit().

🤖 Generated with Codebuff
Co-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
